# Mode three, CR 608.2b: Bot2 returns Bot1's Elvish Mystic to its owner's hand in response (Unsummon), so the creature you
# control is an illegal target as the Charm resolves: no counter is put (it would be on nothing) and nothing fights, so the
# Llanowar Elves, still a legal target, are undamaged.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Elvish Mystic
Vigorbloom Charm
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Llanowar Elves
Unsummon
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Vigorbloom Charm.Cast
Bot1.Modes(3)
Bot1.Target(Elvish Mystic)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Unsummon.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Pearl
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Unsummon
Stack.Count = 0
